Detailed Component Configuration
1. Variables (variables.tf)
Defines configurable deployment parameters, allowing dynamic target bucket naming:

Terraform
variable "KKE_BUCKET" {
  type        = string
  description = "The name of the new S3 bucket destination"
  default     = "devops-sync-374084099"
}
2. Infrastructure & Data Migration (main.tf)
Bucket Provisioning: Dynamically provisions the destination S3 bucket using the KKE_BUCKET variable.

Security & Access Control: Enforces BucketOwnerPreferred ownership controls and configures a private canned ACL.

Automated Data Sync: Triggers an idempotent aws s3 sync operation via a null_resource execution block to copy all objects seamlessly from the source bucket (devops-s3-374084099) to the target destination.

3. Outputs (outputs.tf)
Exposes critical deployment metadata for post-apply validation:

new_kke_bucket_name: Returns the unique name of the created S3 bucket.

new_kke_bucket_acl: Returns the active access control list configuration (private).

Deployment & Verification Guide
Initialize Terraform:

Bash
terraform init -upgrade
Apply Infrastructure Configuration:

Bash
terraform apply --auto-approve
Verify State & Infrastructure Consistency:
Ensure zero configuration drift by running:

Bash
terraform plan
Expected Output:

Plaintext
No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.
